      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-livida-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<ul><li>Wild-caught from Indonesia.</li><li>Belongs to the Betta coccina complex.</li><li>IUCN Red List: Endangered (a very high risk of extinction in the wild).</li><li>Maximum size: 3 - 4 cm (1.2 - 1.5 inches).</li><li>TDS: 60 - 100.</li><li>pH: 5.0 - 6.5.</li><li>Temperature: 24 - 28°C (75 - 82°F).</li><li>Breeding: bubble nester.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-livida-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Have the habitat ready before purchase.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-livida-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Betta livida belongs to the Betta coccina complex. It has a dark red body with specks of metallic yellow/green. Some have a dark green spot in the centre of the body. Like most coccinas, they have reflective blue eyes.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-livida-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Recommended 1 pair per 5 gallons (about 19 litres).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-livida-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<ul><li>TDS: 60 - 100</li><li>pH: 5.0 - 6.5</li><li>Temperature: 24 - 28°C (75 - 82°F)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-livida-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Fed live blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-livida-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Moderately aggressive; males can be territorial when establishing breeding grounds. Because of their small size, multiple pairs can be kept as long as there is enough space and cover. Expect fin nipping.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-livida-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Bubble nester.</p>"
    }
